      "text": "To solve this problem, let's analyze the growth pattern of the bacteria colony. The colony starts with 3 bacteria and doubles every day. We need to determine the day on which the colony first has more than 100 bacteria.\n\n1. **Day 0 (initial condition):**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of bacteria} = 3\n   \\]\n\n2. **Day 1:**\n   The number of bacteria doubles.\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 2 = 6\n   \\]\n\n3. **Day 2:**\n   The number of bacteria doubles again.\n   \\[\n   6 \\times 2 = 12\n   \\]\n\n4. **Day 3:**\n   The number of bacteria doubles again.\n   \\[\n   12 \\times 2 = 24\n   \\]\n\n5. **Day 4:**\n   The number of bacteria doubles again.\n   \\[\n   24 \\times 2 = 48\n   \\]\n\n6. **Day 5:**\n   The number of bacteria doubles again.\n   \\[\n   48 \\times 2 = 96\n   \\]\n\n7. **Day 6:**\n   The number of bacteria doubles again.\n   \\[\n   96 \\times 2 = 192\n   \\]\n\nOn Day 6, the colony has 192 bacteria, which is more than 100 bacteria. Therefore, the first day on which the colony has more than 100 bacteria is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).",
